menu "Networking"

config NET_WIFI
    bool "Wi-Fi (station + SoftAP)"
    default y
    help
      Compiles the cyw43 station/AP state machine, the /api/wifi routes and
      the credential store in or out entirely. The Bluetooth stack shares the
      same CYW43439 but does not depend on this: a BLE-only build is valid and
      is reachable over USB-NCM.

config NET_USB_NCM
    bool "USB-NCM (Ethernet over the USB cable)"
    default y
    help
      A network interface over the target's own USB port. Worth keeping even
      on a Wi-Fi build: it is reachable before Wi-Fi is configured and when the
      access point is down, which is the difference between a bad Wi-Fi setting
      being an annoyance and being a reflash.

comment "USB-NCM /24: device takes .1, the host is handed .16 by DHCP."
comment "MUST NOT collide with another NCM device on the same host -- the bench"
comment "this was developed on already had an unrelated project on 192.168.7.x,"
comment "and two NCM interfaces sharing a subnet is a routing coin-toss."

config NET_NCM_IP0
    int "USB-NCM subnet octet 1"
    depends on NET_USB_NCM
    default 192

config NET_NCM_IP1
    int "USB-NCM subnet octet 2"
    depends on NET_USB_NCM
    default 168

config NET_NCM_IP2
    int "USB-NCM subnet octet 3"
    depends on NET_USB_NCM
    default 8

config NET_MDNS
    bool "mDNS responder"
    default y

config NET_HOSTNAME
    string "mDNS / DHCP hostname"
    default "bluetooth-rp2-webapp"
    help
      The project name, spelled as a DNS label: a hostname may contain only
      letters, digits and hyphens, so the underscores in "bluetooth_rp2_webapp"
      become hyphens. Reachable as <name>.local once mDNS is up.

config LWIP_MEM_SIZE_KB
    int "lwIP heap (KB)"
    default 48
    help
      lwIP's transmit heap. 48 KB suits RP2350's 520 KB SRAM; drop to 32 on an
      RP2040. Every other lwIP setting lives in include/lwipopts.h and must be
      changed there, never as a -D: those are unconditional #defines and win
      silently.

endmenu
